{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "TriageWiseProdrome — patient detail cases (get_patient_detail + GET /intakes/{id}, reqs detail endpoint / R1 mode / D1 surface)",
    "validates": "Two SEPARATE layers, tested independently: (A) SERVICE composition — TriageService.get_patient_detail(intake_id) assembles a PatientDetail domain object from stored rows; (B) ENDPOINT response — GET /intakes/{id}?mode=... emits PatientDetailOut JSON, with black-box stripping.",
    "nature": "INTEGRATION. Seed rows, then either call the service (layer A) OR hit the endpoint (layer B). Each case targets ONE layer — never mixes domain-object assertions with emitted-JSON assertions.",
    "layer_key": {
      "service": "assert on the PatientDetail OBJECT: domain types (Driver/Trigger objects), domain attr casing (system_ESI), missing_fields present, override=None when absent. No status_code, no event (the service alone logs nothing).",
      "endpoint": "assert on the emitted JSON from PatientDetailOut.model_dump(exclude_none=True): response casing (system_esi), DriverOut/RedFlagOut DICTS (not domain types), fields ABSENT (not null) when stripped, status_code, explanation_viewed event (route fires it in xai only)."
    },
    "notes": [
      "band_name derived via LABEL_MAP from ESI.",
      "severity_score may serialize as float (e.g. 9.0) if the column is float — endpoint cases assert numeric equality, not int identity.",
      "exclude_none: a stripped OR genuinely-absent field is OMITTED from JSON, never null.",
      "explanation_viewed fires in the ROUTE, xai branch only — so it's an endpoint-layer assertion, never a service-layer one.",
      "mode is a required query param - a request without it fails validation and returns 400 invalid_input (the app normalizes all validation errors to 400, not 422).",
      "base_rate_line is xai-only: absent in blackbox (in fields_absent), and present in xai ONLY when the complaint matches a condition_reference row (else None -> omitted).",
      "data_completeness is now a TOP-LEVEL always-shown field (severity box, both modes). risk_blurb is xai-only (names drivers -> reasoning): present in xai, absent in blackbox."
    ],
    "band_label_map": {
      "ESI-1": "Critical",
      "ESI-2": "Emergent",
      "ESI-3": "Urgent",
      "ESI-4": "Less urgent",
      "ESI-5": "Non-urgent"
    }
  },
